================================================================================
REPRO INVESTIGATION — deploy-web-admin.sh scp/atomic-swap race
Date: 2026-05-13
Branch: fix/deploy-web-admin-atomic-swap-race
Investigator: chat2 dispatched per MO
================================================================================

ORIGINAL FAILURE MODE (per MO context, observed 3x in one evening)
------------------------------------------------------------------
- "[3/4] 上传到 139" prints "✓ 上传完成"
- Immediately after, "[4/4] atomic swap" heredoc fails with:
    tar: /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz: Cannot open: No such file or directory
- Manual scp + atomic-swap chain works 100% (serial, single-threaded)
- Recovery: cleanup + retry. scp ~100s for 3MB.


HYPOTHESIS RANKING & ELIMINATION
--------------------------------
H1: scp -q silent failure with set -e not catching
    REJECTED — script line 31 has `set -e`. If scp returned non-zero, bash
    would exit IMMEDIATELY after scp (line 197), NEVER printing "✓ 上传完成"
    on line 198. Yet the "✓" message is observed. So scp returned exit 0.

H2: /tmp on 139 has parallel cleaner deleting tarball mid-flight
    REJECTED — server forensics:
      - systemd-tmpfiles-clean.timer is DAILY (next: 17h from check time)
      - No cron.d/* or cron.daily/* references to tmp cleanup
      - /tmp on /dev/vda3 ext4 (regular FS, not tmpfs) — durable file
      - 15G free on / partition — no disk pressure
      A daily cleanup cannot kill a 3MB file 1-3s after it lands.

H3: ssh ControlMaster session mux issue
    REJECTED — no ~/.ssh/config exists on operator machine. ControlMaster
    is OFF. Each ssh/scp opens a fresh connection.

H4: File buffering (sync barrier missing post-scp)
    REJECTED — /tmp is ext4 on a regular block device. scp closes its
    SSH channel after completion; sshd flushes the file. The next ssh
    connection opens a fresh file handle and would see the file. No
    NFS, no weird caching layer.

H5 (NEW, identified during analysis): Concurrent-deploy collision on shared
    remote path /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz
    ACCEPTED — the script uses a HARDCODED, NON-UNIQUE remote path.
    All 5 hardcoded references in the original script:
        L197: scp -q "$TMP_TAR" "$GATEWAY:/tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz"
        L214: tar xzf /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz   (test heredoc)
        L238: rm -f /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz     (test cleanup)
        L277: scp -q ... :/tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz   (prod)
        L292: tar xzf /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz   (prod heredoc)
        L312: rm -f /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz     (prod cleanup)

    Race timeline that produces the observed symptom:
        T+0.0s  Deploy A: scp succeeds, file at /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz
        T+0.5s  Deploy A: prints "✓ 上传完成"
        T+1.0s  Deploy B: scp succeeds (overwrites same file)
        T+1.2s  Deploy B: heredoc tar+swap completes
        T+1.5s  Deploy B: heredoc rm -f /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz
        T+1.8s  Deploy A: heredoc tar xzf /tmp/web-admin-dist.tar.gz
                          → "Cannot open: No such file or directory"

    Matches symptom EXACTLY:
      - "✓ 上传完成" prints (scp DID succeed at A's T+0.5s)
      - tar fails (B's rm beat A's tar in the ~1-3s gap)
      - Manual single-threaded works (no concurrent deploy)
      - 30-50% failure rate matches typical interleaving probability when
        2-3 deploys fire in close succession during a busy day


SERIAL REPRO: NOT POSSIBLE
--------------------------
The race requires 2+ concurrent deploys. A single sequential invocation
CANNOT trigger it because there's no second process to rm the file.
This is consistent with operator's observation: "Manual scp + atomic
swap 100% works."

WHY THE BUG SURFACED MAY 13 SPECIFICALLY
----------------------------------------
Per MEMORY.md (May 13 organizer session):
- "~45 PRs" merged in one day
- "6+ prod deploys"
- "0 concurrent-edit incidents post-round 3" (concurrency was top-of-mind)
- "Disk-full incident (~160GB freed by removing 199 stale worktrees)"

A busy organizer day with rapid back-to-back deploys + multiple worktrees
made the previously-latent race finally visible. Until May 13, deploys
were serial enough that two deploys' [scp...tar...rm] windows didn't
overlap.


FIX DESIGN
----------
1. Per-PID remote path: REMOTE_TAR="/tmp/web-admin-dist.$$.tar.gz"
   - $$ = bash PID of the deploy script
   - Each deploy gets its own unique remote tarball
   - Concurrent deploys can no longer rm each other's files
   - Eliminates the root cause completely

2. Post-scp verify (defense-in-depth):
   - LOCAL_SIZE  = stat -c %s "$TMP_TAR"
   - REMOTE_SIZE = ssh ... stat -c %s "$REMOTE_TAR"  (or "MISSING")
   - If mismatch → abort BEFORE atomic-swap heredoc with clear error
   - Catches future failure modes (partial transfer, /tmp full,
     misconfiguration) with a precise error instead of opaque
     "Cannot open" downstream

Fix scope: 6 hardcoded path references replaced with $REMOTE_TAR;
2 verify blocks added (one for test path, one for --env all prod path).
No retry loop (intentional — eliminating the root cause makes retry
unnecessary; can add later if a different transient mode appears).
